From: TNG Technical Manual compatibility investigation
Subject: [PATCH] DIRECTOR: restore Trek Tech passive hover screens

Trek Tech's Index and Help screens deliberately use passive text and guide
sprites as mouseCast targets. The title-specific full-row menu workaround
filters mouseCast to mouse-responsive sprites, which is correct on ordinary
topic screens but makes Index highlighting and Help descriptions stop tracking
the pointer.

Use Director's ordinary topmost-sprite hit test only while the Index is active
or the current marker is a Help screen. Keep the filtered hit test everywhere
else so the restored full-width topic menus are unaffected.
---
 engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp
--- a/engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp
+++ b/engines/director/lingo/lingo-the.cpp
@@ -843,12 +843,21 @@ Datum Lingo::getTheEntity(int entity, Datum &id, int field) {
 		{
 			// TODO: How is this handled with multiple casts in D5?
 			Common::Point pos = g_director->getCurrentWindow()->getMousePos();
+			const bool trekTech = Common::String(g_director->getGameId()).equals("trektech");
+			bool passiveHoverScreen = false;
+			if (trekTech) {
+				Common::String marker = score->getFrameLabel(score->getCurrentLabelNumber());
+				passiveHoverScreen = marker.hasPrefixIgnoreCase("help");
+				if (g_lingo->_globalvars.contains("gImInIndex") &&
+						g_lingo->_globalvars["gImInIndex"].asInt())
+					passiveHoverScreen = true;
+			}
 			// Trek Tech stamps its topic bars onto the stage, then handles the
 			// complete rows through a global coordinate-zone script. Decorative
 			// sprites over the text must not make mouseCast report a cast member,
 			// or that authored handler only receives clicks in the small square.
-			uint16 spriteId = Common::String(g_director->getGameId()).equals("trektech") ?
-					score->getMouseSpriteIDFromPos(pos) : score->getSpriteIDFromPos(pos);
+			uint16 spriteId = trekTech && !passiveHoverScreen ?
+					score->getMouseSpriteIDFromPos(pos) : score->getSpriteIDFromPos(pos);
 			if (spriteId) {
 				d = score->getSpriteById(spriteId)->_castId.toMultiplex();
 			} else {
